{"id":"chatcmpl-3541a522-1e0e-43e1-9b0a-500f99ec3024","object":"chat.completion","created":1795244738,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When the imaging projection (lateral) makes the key discriminating feature (laterality) hard to assess, the successful strategy was to triangulate across multiple independent vision-language models rather than trust any single read. Conflicting or null outputs from one model were treated as signals to seek additional evidence, and a verifier was used to explicitly flag the projection's limitation before committing to a forced-choice answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When the image projection obscures the discriminating feature, query multiple independent models and use consensus rather than a single read.\",\n    \"Treat a model reporting 'no finding' when options imply a finding exists as a cue to cross-check with alternate models, not to conclude absence.\",\n    \"Use a verification step to explicitly state the projection's limitation (e.g., laterality unreliable on lateral view) before finalizing a forced-choice answer.\",\n    \"When forced-choice options exist and evidence is ambiguous, select the answer best supported by cross-model consensus while documenting the uncertainty.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Cross-check findings across 2-3 independent vision-language models; use a verifier to flag projection/technique limitations; prefer consensus over single-model claims.\",\n    \"Ambiguous forced-choice tasks\": \"When the correct answer must be one of N options but evidence is weak, gather multiple independent assessments and pick the best-supported option while noting residual uncertainty.\",\n    \"Conflicting model outputs\": \"Do not default to the first model; escalate to additional models and a verification step, and weight outputs by whether they acknowledge the task's inherent limitations.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm whether the imaging projection/technique can even resolve the discriminating feature before trusting any laterality or localization claim.\",\n    \"Require at least two independent model agreements (or a verifier endorsement) before committing to a forced-choice answer under ambiguity.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":776,"total_tokens":1173,"completion_tokens":397,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":776},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":397}}}